### Food Delivery Platform - AI MCP Server (agent loop, tools, MCP endpoint)
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
###
### These are SERVER-TO-SERVER calls: the browser uses /api/v1/assistant/** (ai-mcp-client). Every /internal and /mcp call needs
### X-Service-Token (env AI_SERVICE_TOKEN; the dev profile default is below) and, to act for someone, their access token
### (Authorization: Bearer, normally forwarded by ai-mcp-client; here from a sign-in through the gateway, valid 15 min).
### Needs: Ollama with the model (OLLAMA_MODEL), Redis (proposals) and the API Gateway with the services behind it.

@service = http://localhost:8098
@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@token = dev-ai-service-token
@customerEmail = meera.iyer@example.com
@customerPassword = Meera1234
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123
@ownerEmail = test.owner@fooddelivery.local
@ownerPassword = Test@12345
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@ownerToken = {{ownerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Sign-ins -> access tokens (run again after 15 minutes)
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{customerEmail}}", "password": "{{customerPassword}}", "role": "CUSTOMER" }

###
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}", "role": "PLATFORM_ADMIN" }

###
# @name ownerLogin
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{ownerEmail}}", "password": "{{ownerPassword}}", "role": "RESTAURANT_ADMIN" }


### Is the model available? (no identity needed beyond the token)
GET {{service}}/internal/agent/status
X-Service-Token: {{token}}

### Admin: a question answered with the admin tools (first answer can take a minute on a CPU)
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Request-Id: http-sample-1

{
  "message": "How many orders were delivered today, and how many were cancelled?",
  "history": []
}

### Owner: sales of my restaurants
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

{
  "message": "Which dishes sold the most this week?",
  "history": [
    {"role": "USER", "text": "Hi"},
    {"role": "ASSISTANT", "text": "Hello! How can I help with your restaurant?"}
  ]
}

### Customer: search, then prepare an order. The answer carries "pendingAction" with an actionId.
# @name prepare
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{
  "message": "Order 2 chicken biryani from restaurant 1 to my default address, cash on delivery",
  "history": []
}

### Confirm the proposal (what the Confirm button does; repeating it returns the same order: ALREADY_CREATED)
@actionId = {{prepare.response.body.$.pendingAction.actionId}}
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/actions/{{actionId}}/confirm
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Cancel a proposal instead (204)
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/actions/{{actionId}}/cancel
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### No service token: 401
POST {{service}}/internal/agent/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

{ "message": "hello", "history": [] }

### MCP (Streamable HTTP): initialize. An MCP host sends the same headers (service token + access token) on every request.
POST {{service}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
X-Service-Token: {{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-03-26",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "rest-client", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}
